      "description": "The NOAA Multi-Radar/Multi-Sensor System (MRMS) integrates data from multiple radars and radar networks, surface observations, numerical weather prediction (NWP) models, and climatology to generate seamless, high spatio-temporal resolution mosaics at low latency focused on hail, wind, tornado, quantitative precipitation estimations, convection, icing, and turbulence. These datasets have been translated to cloud-optimized Icechunk Zarr format by [dynamical.org](https://dynamical.org). - [NOAA MRMS CONUS analysis, hourly](https://dynamical.org/catalog/noaa-mrms-conus-analysis-hourly/) - Hourly precipitation analysis from the Multi-Radar Multi-Sensor (MRMS) system operated by NOAA NWS NCEP.",
